-- title:
--   Transversality at a crossing: branch ideals sum to the maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$ and let $\mathfrak X$ be a `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundling of the properness, flatness, integrality, normality, rational- and geometric-model, section and smooth-locus data for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the modular function field over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O$ for `baseChangeO p O`, the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two component maps $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$, and let $x_n = \mathfrak X.\mathrm{crossingPt}\,O\,\kappa\,\mathrm{to}\kappa\,n$ be its image in $X_O$ under the first projection followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`. Let $\xi_\infty = \mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{inf}\,O\,\kappa\,\mathrm{to}\kappa$ and $\xi_0 = \mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{zero}\,O\,\kappa\,\mathrm{to}\kappa$ be the two points of $X_O$ attached to the two components of the characteristic-$p$ fibre, and assume $\xi_\infty \rightsquigarrow x_n$ and $\xi_0 \rightsquigarrow x_n$. For a specialisation $\xi \rightsquigarrow x$ the branch ideal `Scheme.branchIdeal` is the preimage, along the specialisation map $\mathcal O_{X,x} \to \mathcal O_{X,\xi}$ of stalks, of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,\xi}$. The assertion is that the sum of the branch ideals of the two given specialisations equals the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal O_{X_O,x_n}$.
--
--   This is the transversality statement at a crossing point of the Deligne–Rapoport special fibre: the two branches through $x_n$ meet transversally, so that the two branch ideals already generate the maximal ideal of the local ring at the crossing. It is used to produce a pair of generators of the branch ideals and, from there, oriented crossing charts at such points.
